{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>Vengeance is Mine, and recompense.</b> This may be explained along the lines of what they said, of blessed memory (Avodah Zarah 3a), that in the future to come HaShem will bring forth the sun from its sheath: the wicked are judged by it and it burns them, while the righteous are healed by it. And this is what the verse says: ״לִי נָקָם וְשִׁלֵּם״ — meaning: נָקָם (vengeance) upon the wicked, and שִׁלֵּם (recompense) of good reward to the righteous." "<b>When their foot slips.</b> This is the sod of the statement (Sotah 49a) ״עִקְּבוֹת מְשִׁיחָא״ — it is the sifting of the sparks from the feet of Samael, when the רַגְלָם (their feet) of the doers of wickedness slip, and that which cleaved to them from the force that sustains [them] is finished off — as is known to those who know grace (חֵן)." "<b>For near is the day of their calamity, etc.</b> This is the statement of the prophet (Zephaniah 1:7): ״כִּי קָרוֹב יוֹם ה׳״ etc." "<b>And what is poised for them.</b> These are the future consolations: when the doers of wickedness are paid their due, He will immediately hasten to fulfill the future promises to the righteous."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:21:38.544813717Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}